         "Sets how loose a search may be, and answers what it now is.\n"
         "\n"
         "It is what `search` on a list or a map reads, so turn it up to find near\n"
         "misses and down to insist on the exact thing."
         ,
         "satellite.system.threshold(6)\n"
         "satellite.console.display(satellite.system.threshold())"
         )

// 1 22 7  satellite.system.persist()
SAT_HELP(SYSTEM_PERSIST_0, SYSTEM_PERSIST_0,
         "Answers whether the prompt is keeping what each line declares.\n"
         "\n"
         "It is on to begin with, which is why a variable you declare at the prompt\n"
         "is still there on the next line."
         ,
         "satellite.console.display(satellite.system.persist())"
         )

// 1 22 8  satellite.system.persist(x)
SAT_HELP(SYSTEM_PERSIST_X, SYSTEM_PERSIST_0,
         "Turns the prompt's memory of declarations on or off, and answers what it\n"
         "now is.\n"
         "\n"
         "Turning it off does not throw away what is already held; it stops the next\n"
         "line adding to it, so a program can switch it off around one line and back\n"
         "on afterwards. It wants a real bool, so write\n"
         "`satellite.bool.false` rather than a bare word."
         ,
         "satellite.console.display(satellite.system.persist(satellite.bool.false))\n"
         "satellite.console.display(satellite.system.persist(satellite.bool.true))"
         )

